                   this header fixed that but left it far from the range. Only
                   the line views have energy on the horizontal axis -- the maps
                   carry it vertically on a grid the drawing code assumes
                   uniform, and a uniform eV grid is NOT uniform in lambda, so
                   the toggle hides itself there rather than misdrawing. -->
              <div class="chart-header">
                <span class="chart-title" id="efd-chart-main-title">Cross section vs energy</span>
                {/* Which polarizabilities to draw, beside the title they
                    belong to. The buttons are built from the payload, not
                    hard-coded: a run with orders = shg has no third harmonic
                    to offer, and offering one would be a lie about what was
                    computed. */}
                {/* Both are absolute, and which one you want depends on
                    what you are comparing: sigma per unit length is the
                    physical cross section of a ribbon, sigma over its width is
                    the efficiency, which is what the plasmonic-nanoparticles
                    lab plots and what compares across widths. */}
                <div class="efd-chart-pick efd-obs-only" data-obs-for="spectrum" hidden>
                  <div class="plot-tabs plot-tabs--toolbar" id="efd-xs-unit" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Cross section units">
                    <button class="plot-tab active" type="button" data-xs="area" role="radio" aria-checked="true">&sigma;/area</button>
                    <button class="plot-tab" type="button" data-xs="nm" role="radio" aria-checked="false">&sigma; (nm)</button>
                  </div>
                </div>
                {/* The drive, drawn over the field it produced: the
                    electron's trajectory or the dipole and its axis. Purely a
