                  <span>Source</span>
                </label>
                {/* TWO ways to see the same modes, each with its own switch,
                    because they are two different calculations and the point of
                    the panel is to compare them. Level 3 reads the ridges off
                    this map; Level 2 root-finds the bands without ever seeing
                    it. The map's own tracks are on by default -- they come free
                    with the run that drew the map. The Level 2 bands are off:
                    the first tick costs a second calculation.

                    "beta = 0" is in the label, not in a footnote, because the
                    bands are ALWAYS solved with drift off -- with drift, eta is
                    a tensor and a Level 2 band spectrum does not exist. At
                    beta = 0 the label is merely redundant; at beta != 0 it is
                    the whole caveat, and a label that is true at one setting
                    and silent at the other is the one that misleads. */}
                <label class="efd-chart-check efd-obs-only" data-obs-for="ldos" hidden>
                  <input type="checkbox" id="efd-ldos-peaks" checked>
